hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2888","\n I read to Ahmad ibn Abi Suraikh that 'Amr ibn Mujammic informed them on the authority of Musa ibn 'Uqba, who narrated from Nafi', who narrated from Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was mounted on his mount and it stood up at the mosque of Dhul-Hulaifa during Hajj or 'Umrah"","" he would pronounce the Talbiyah.\"" He then mentioned the hadith in full and said: \""Then he would"""""
